{
    "test_name": "MOB.396_Work_Create_From_Asset",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.396_Work_Create_From_Asset",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.396` Create a work order from a **Mobile Job asset** \u2014 the `Add Work` button on the\nfull-page asset detail (`AssetDetails.tsx:78`, `AddWorkButton defaultAsset={asset}`).\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **LEAVES RESIDUE**: a real work order per run, undeletable from mobile, tagged\n  `DD SYNTHETIC MOBILE`. Approved by the repo owner 2026-08-12.\n- One of the **four** real create entry points (Mobile Map \u00b7 Mobile Job asset \u00b7 Asset\n  Lookup \u00b7 Work Orders). The inherited *Asset Register* and *Hierarchy* entries do not\n  exist in mobile.\n- What is NEW versus MOB.300 is only the entry point and the pre-bound asset \u2014 same form,\n  same mutation \u2014 so this stays deliberately thin rather than re-testing the form.\n- Modal-close is genuine proof (trap 6): the insert form closes inside Apollo's\n  `update()` with no `optimisticResponse`, the same shape MOB.300 relies on.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Work Order",
            "CRUD",
            "residue"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                },
                {
                    "name": "RUNID",
                    "type": "text",
                    "pattern": "{{ numeric(8) }}",
                    "example": "48120735"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
